{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>וכל</b>. יכתו — from the root of doubling." "<b>אתנניה</b> — what they gave to idols for prostitution in place of HaShem. The Nagid said: כי קבצה ought to have had a qof with shureq, and likewise: ופתחו שעריך תמיד, ויישם בארון, על בשר אדם לא ייסך. And in my opinion: קבצה שומרון and פתחו are pausal forms, like אשר ילדה אותם and ויאמר ליוסף and likewise ויישם אותו המשים and likewise לא ייסך הכהן." "And the meaning of עד אתנן זונה ישובו — the gold and silver of idols, to the idols of Assyria."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma וכל is not part of this comment, which addresses the form יכתו in the preceding clause.", 1 "Resolved הנגיד as 'the Nagid' (likely Samuel ibn Naghrilla, or possibly a different medieval grammarian by that epithet). His argument is highly compressed and the logic of the biblical examples cited is not articulated; translated as preserved."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:37.696831325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}